$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for direct C-2 arylation of
N-methyl-7-azaindole (Procedure A) 1-Methyl
2-phenyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine (2a): N-Methyl-7-azaindole (100 mg,
0.757 mmol), phenylboronic acid (110.9 mg, 0.909 mmol), Pd(OAC)2 (8.5 mg
0.037 mmol), PPh3 (19.8 mg 0.037 mmol), and Na2S2O8 (270.5 mg 1.136
mmol), were added to a round bottom flask. AcOH (2 mL) was added by
syringe. The flask was kept open and the reaction mixture was stirred for
4-5 h in air at room temperature. The progress of the reaction was
monitored by TLC and after completion of the reaction, AcOH was recovered
by distillation under reduced pressure and the residue was dissolved in
CH2Cl2 (50 mL) and washed with aqueous NaHCO3 (2 x 15 mL). The combined
organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 and concentrated under vacuum. The
crude product was purified by silica gel column chromatography
(hexane/EtOAc, 98:2). The desired product 2a ( 118.2 mg, 75%) as a
colorless liquid.
2-(Benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-yl)-5-bromo-1-methyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine
(2q) Synthesized from 5-bromo1-methyl-1H-pyrrolo[2,3-b]pyridine (150 mg,
0.710 mmol) benzo[d][1,3]dioxol-5-ylboronic acid (141.6 mg, 0.85 mmol),
Pd(OAC)2 (7.9 mg, 5 mol %), PPh3 (18.6 mg, 10 mol %), Na2S2O8 (253.7 mg,
1.065 mmol), by following procedure A. Purified by silica gel column
chromatography (hexane/EtOAc, 96: 4). Compound 2q (176.5 mg, 75%) as a
white solid. mp 142-143 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.33 (d, J = 1.1
Hz, 1H), 7.99 (d, J = 1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.00 (d, J = 10.1 Hz, 2H), 6.94 (s,
1H), 6.39 (s, 1H), 6.05 (s, 2H), 3.82 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ
148.1, 147.5, 143.0, 142.9, 129.9, 125.5, 123.1, 122.0, 111.8, 109.4,
108.6, 101.4, 98.5, 29.9; HRMS (ESI): calcd for C15H12BrN2O2 [M+H]+:
331.0077, found: 331.0072.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
