$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-(8-bromo-2,3-diphenylquinoxalin-5-yl)thiophene-2-carbaldehyde (2)
Compound 1 (1.06 g, 2.4 mmol), 10 mL of 2.0 M K2CO3 aqueous solution and
a catalytic amount Pd(PPh3)4 (5 mole %) in 20 mL THF were heated to
reflux for 0.5 h and then injected 10 mL THF containing
(5-formylthiophen-2-yl)boronic acid (300 mg, 1.9 mmol). After refluxed
for 12 h, the mixture was poured into water and extracted with CH2Cl2
(3x10 mL). The organic portion was combined and removed by rotary
evaporation. The residue was purified by column chromatography on silica
using dichloromethane as eluent.
5-(8-(4-(4-(2,2-bis(2',4'-bis(hexyloxy)-[1,1'-biphenyl]-4-yl)vinyl)phenyl)-1,2,3,3a,4,8b-hexahydrocyclopenta[b]indo7-yl)-2,3-diphenylquinoxalin-5-yl)thiophene-2-carbal
dehyde (4) The synthesis method resembles that of compound 3 and the
compound was purified by silica gel column chromatography with DCM to
give a red solid (yield 75%). 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz), δ (TMS, ppm):
0.79-0.96 (m, 12H), 1.23-1.38 (m, 16H), 1.39-1.45 (m, 4H), 1.45-1.54 (m,
4H), 1.58-1.67 (m, 1H), 1.70-1.85 (m, 9H), 1.86-1.92 (m, 1H), 1.93-2.01
(m, 1H), 2.02-2.18 (m, 2H), 3.90-4.04 (m, 9H), 4.78-4.84 (m, 1H),
6.53-6.60 (m, 4H), 7.01 (s, 1H), 7.10-7.19 (m, 5H), 7.27-7.40 (m, 8H),
7.40-7.44 (m, 4H), 7.48-7.52 (m, 2H), 7.55-7.62 (m, 3H), 7.62-7.67 (m,
2H), 7.73-7.78 (m, 3H), 7.83 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 7.87 (d, J = 7.9 Hz,
1H), 7.93 (d, J = 4.0 Hz, 1H), 8.23 (d, J = 7.9 Hz, 1H), 9.99 (s, 1H).
13C NMR (CDCl3, 100 MHz), δ (TMS, ppm): 14.0, 14.1, 22.6, 24.6, 25.8,
29.1, 29.3, 31.4, 31.5, 31.6, 34.0, 34.8, 45.5, 68.1, 68.4, 68.9, 100.5,
105.3, 105.4, 108.3, 118.1, 123.2, 126.7, 126.9, 127.2, 127.9, 128.2,
128.3, 128.4, 128.6, 128.9, 129.0, 129.2, 129.3, 129.8, 129.9, 130.2,
130.4, 130.5, 130.8, 131.0, 131.1, 135.0, 135.8, 137.5, 138.6, 138.9,
140.2, 141.2, 141.3, 141.6, 144.6, 147.0, 149.0, 149.1, 151.7, 151.8,
157.1, 159.8, 183.4. HRMS (APCI, m/z): [M+H]+ calcd. for (C92H98N3O5S):
1356.7228; found: 1356.7225.
