$DATUM 2,5-dioxopyrrolidin-1-yl-5'-(7-(thiophen-2-yl)benzo[c][1,2,5]thiadiazol-4-yl)2-2'bithiophene-5-carboxylate
(5). A mixture of compound 2c (0.38 g, 1 mmol), 2f (2 mmol), (PPh3)2PdCl2
(0.05 mmol) and NaHCO3 (1 mmol) in DMF/H2O (2:1, 3 mL) was irradiated
with microwaves at 80°C for 5 min. The reaction mixture was brought to
room temperature and the solvent was evaporated under reduced pressure.
The product was isolated by flash chromatography on florisil with
increasing amounts of CH2Cl2 in Petroleum ether as eluent. Yield 75%
(0.392 g). Red purple solid. mp=175°C; EI-MS m/z 523 (M+); 1H NMR (400
MHz, CDCl3, TMS/ppm): δ 8.15 (dd, 3J=3.6 Hz, 4J=1.2 Hz, 1H), 8.05 (d,
J=4, 1H), 7.96 (d, J=4, 1H), 7.90 (s, 2H), 7.48 (dd, 3J=5.2 Hz, 4J=1.2
Hz, 1H), 7.44 (d, J=4, 1H), 7.33 (d, J=4, 1H), 7.23 (dd, 3J=5.2 Hz,
3J=3.6 Hz, 1H), 2.91 (s, 4H); 1H NMR (400 MHz, DMSO, 50°C): δ 8.14 (m,
5H), 7.75 (m, 2H), 7.63 (d, J=4, 1H), 7.26 (dd, 3J=4.8 Hz, 4J=4 Hz, 1H),
2.89 (s, 4H); 13C NMR (400 MHz, DMSO, 50°C): δ 170.0, 156.8, 151.5,
151.4, 146.5, 140.1, 138.25, 138.16, 135.8, 128.4, 128.3, 128.0, 127.8,
127.6, 126.2, 125.8, 125.6, 125.5, 123.8, 123.3, 25.4; UV/Vis: λmax 479
nm (ε 26142 cm-1 M-1), λem. 613 nm in DMSO.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
