$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: S8-7.
2-(5-(5-(HBQA-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)-5,5-dimethyl-1,3-dioxane
(8) To a stirred solution of 2 (0.22 g, 0.49 mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (0.028
g, 0.024 mmol) in tetrahydrofuran (10 mL) was added
4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-2-(5-(5-(5,5-dimethyl-1,3-dioxan-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)-1,3,2-dioxaborolane
(0.89 g, 2.19 mmol), potassium carbonate (2.76 g, 20 mmol) in THF (15 mL)
and H2O (10 mL). The mixture was refluxed for 18 h. After cooling the
solution, H2O (30 ml) was added to the solution and extracted by
dichloromethane (30 mL × 3). The organic layer was separated and dried in
MgSO4. The solvent was removed in vacuo. The pure product 8 was obtained
by silica gel chromatography using a mixture of methylene chloride and
n-hexane (1:1) as an eluent. S8-8.
2-(5-(5-(6,10-Dihexyloxy-HBQA-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)thiophen-2-yl)-5,5-dimethyl-1,3-dioxane
(9) The product was synthesized according to the procedure as described
above for synthesis of 8, giving a yellow solid of the product 9 in 75 %
yield. Mp: 176 °C. 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ 7.58 (s, 2H), 7.21 (m, 5H), 7.18 (d,
1H, J = 3.6 Hz), 7.10 (d, 1H, J = 3.6 Hz), 7.07 (d, 1H, J = 3.6 Hz), 5.65
(s, 1H), 4.05 (t, 4H, J = 7.5 Hz), 3.73 (m, 4H), 1.69 (s, 12H), 1.68 (s,
6H), 1.67 (m, 4H), 1.43 - 1.30 (m, 12H), 1.33 (s, 3H), 0.93 (t, 6H, J =
6.9 Hz), 0.83 (s, 3H). 13C NMR (CDCl3): δ 144.1, 139.8, 137.1, 135.3,
132.1, 130.1, 129.9, 129.5, 128.0, 125.8, 124.7, 123.9, 123.4, 122.6,
120.9, 98.2, 77.5, 35.8, 35.7, 35.5, 33.7, 33.1, 31.8, 31.6, 30.2, 29.2,
23.0, 22.7, 21.9, 14.2. MS: m/z 843.44 [M+]. Anal. Calcd. for
C53H65NO4S2: C, 75.40; H, 7.76. Found: C, 75.16; H, 7.53.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New Type of Organic Sensitizers with a Planar Amine Unit for Efficient
Dye-Sensitized Solar Cells
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Do, Kwangseok; Kim, Duckhyun; Cho, Nara; Paek, Sanghyun; Song, Kihyung;
Ko, Jaejung
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2012), 14(1), 222-225

