$DATUM 2.12. Synthesis of Compound 9 To a THF solution (10 mL) of a mixture of 8
(140 mg, 0.114 mmol) and 3 (202 mg, 0.684 mmol) were successively added
Pd(PPh3)4 (10 mg, 9 μmol) and 4 M aqueous NaOH (1 mL), and the mixture
was refluxed for 12 h under Ar. Then, the reaction mixture was poured
into aqueous NH4Cl, and an aqueous layer separated was extracted with
CH2Cl2. An organic extract was washed with brine, dried over Na2SO4, and
evaporated to dryness under reduced pressure, and the residue was
subjected to flash column chromatography on silica gel using hexane as an
eluent. isolation of 9 as white solid (150 mg, 0.085 mmol, 75%). 1H NMR
(CDCl3, 500 MHz, ppm): δ 7.35 (s, 3H, Ar-H), 7.09 (d, J = 2 Hz, 3H,
Ar-H), 6.96 (s, 3H, Ar-H), 6.78 (d, J = 2 Hz, 3H, Ar-H), 2.80 (t, 6H, J =
7.5 Hz, CH2), 2.73 (t, 6H, J = 7.5 Hz, CH2), 1.72 (t, 6H, J = 7.5 Hz,
CH2), 1.62 (t, 6H, J = 7.5 Hz, CH2), 1.41-1.43 (m, 6H, CH2), 1.17-1.34
(m, 102H, CH2), 0.85-0.89 (m, 18H, CH3). 13C NMR (CDCl3, 125 MHz, ppm): δ
146.1, 144.1, 137.9, 133.4, 132.6, 131.3, 130.8, 129.8, 126.6, 125.3,
121.4, 120.1, 31.9, 31.6, 31.5, 30.3, 30.2, 30.0, 29.7, 29.7, 29.6, 29.6,
29.5, 29.4, 29.4, 29.3, 29.2, 29.0, 22.7, 14.1. MALDI-TOF MS m/z: calcd
for C108H162S9: 1747.0. Found: 1747.0.
