$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 5-(Hexylsulphanyl)-2,2'-bithiophene (4a). A mixture of 2a (1 mmol),
2-thienylboronic acid (3a) (3 mmol), PdCl2dppf (0.05 mmol), KF (4 mmol)
in CH3CN/water 9:1 (3 mL) was irradiated with microwaves at 85°C for 10
min. The reaction mixture was brought to room temperature and the solvent
was evaporated under reduced pressure. The title compound was isolated by
flash chromatography on silica gel in cyclohexane as eluent. Yield 75%.
Yellow oil. 5-(Hexylsulphanyl)-2,2'-bithiophene (4a). Yield 75%. Yellow
oil. EI-MS m/z 282(M+); 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3, TMS/ppm): δ 7.21 (dd,
3J=5.2 Hz, 4J=1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.14 (dd, 3J=4 Hz, 4J=1.2 Hz, 1H), 7.02-7.00
(m, 3H), 2.81 (t, 2H), 1.67- 1.60 (m, 2H), 1.43-1.37 (m, 2H), 1.31-1.26
(m, 4H), 0.88 (m, 3H); 13C NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 140.4, 137.0, 134.1,
133.9, 127.7, 124.5, 123.70, 123.69, 38.9, 31.3, 29.4, 28.1, 22.5, 14.0.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, microwave irradiation (100 W), Suzuki coupling, sealed
glass vessel used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A Successful Chemical Strategy To Induce Oligothiophene Self-Assembly
into Fibers with Tunable Shape and Function
