$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
5-{4-[(Methylsulfonyl)methyl]-6-morpholin-4-ylpyrimidin-2-yl}-1H-indole
(7): Bis(triphenylphosphine)palladium(II) chloride (0.038 g, 0.05 mmol),
compound 62 (0.20 g, 0.69 mmol), 2M Na2CO3 (1.714 ml, 3.43 mmol) and
5-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole (0.167 g, 0.69
mmol) were suspended in 18% DMF in 7:3:2 DME:water:EtOH (6 mL) and sealed
into a microwave tube. The reaction mixture was heated to 95°C for 1 h in
a microwave reactor and then allowed to cool to rt. The mixture was
purified by ion exchange chromatography, using an SCX column. The desired
product was eluted from the column using a solution of 7M NH3 in MeOH.
Fractions containing product were combined and evaporated. The residue
was purified by preparative HPLC using decreasingly polar mixtures of
water (containing 1% NH3) and MeCN as eluents. Fractions containing the
desired compound were combined and evaporated to afford 7. Starting with
76 (200 mg, 0.38 mmol) and 1H-Indole-4-boronic acid (74.1 mg, 0.46 mmol).
Benzyl
4-(1-(2-(1H-indol-4-yl)-6-morpholinopyrimidin-4-yl)cyclopropylsulfonyl)piperidine-1-carboxylate,
yield 172 mg, 75%. 1H NMR (CDCl3): 1.64 - 1.80 (4H, m), 2.13 - 2.41 (2H,
m), 2.48 - 2.64 (2H, m), 3.31 - 3.41 (1H, m), 3.66 - 3.81 (8H, m), 4.09 -
4.27 (2H, m), 5.01 (2H, s), 6.77 (1H, s), 7.20 - 7.30 (5H, m), 7.38 -
7.41 (1H, m), 7.43 - 7.47 (1H, m), 8.11 - 8.14 (1H, m), 8.23 (1H, s).
MS-ESI m/z 602.48 [MH]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, Suzuki coupling, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of
4-{4-[(3R)-3-Methylmorpholin-4-yl]-6-[1-(methylsulfonyl)cyclopropyl]pyrimidin-2-yl}-1H-indole
(AZ20): A Potent and Selective Inhibitor of ATR Protein Kinase with
Monotherapy in Vivo Antitumor Activity
