$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
trans-4-((2-(Butylamino)-5-(3-(morpholinomethyl)pyridin-2-yl)pyrimidin-4-yl)amino)
cyclohexan-1-ol (11) (General Procedure D) A mixture of IVa (45 mg, 0.17
mmol), 4-((2-bromopyridin-3-yl)methyl)morpholine (85 mg, 0.33 mmol),
Pd2(dba)3 (7.6 mg, 0.0080 mmol), PCy3 (6.9 mg, 0.025 mmol), K3PO4 (0.33
mL, 1.0 M solution in deionized water) and butylamine (50 mg, 0.66 mmol)
in a 10 mL microwave tube with dioxane (2.5 mL) was degassed and heated
at 120°C under N2 atmosphere and microwave irradiation for 20 min. The
reaction mixture was diluted with water and extracted with EtOAc (3x).
The combined organic layer was dried (MgSO4) and concentrated.
trans-4-((2-(Butylamino)-5-(4-(morpholinomethyl)pyridin-2-yl)pyrimidin-4-yl)amino)
cyclohexanol (12) The title compound 12 (54.5 mg, 75%) was prepared
according to general procedure D from
4-((2-bromopyridin-4-yl)methyl)morpholine (85.2 mg, 0.33 mmol) as a white
solid. >95% purity. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CD3OD) δ 8.72-8.66 (m, 1H),
8.42-8.34 (m, 1H), 8.04 (s, 1H), 7.52-7.48 (m, 1H), 4.43 (s, 2H),
4.19-4.09 (m, 1H), 3.93-3.83 (m, 3H), 3.70-3.60 (m, 1H), 3.56-3.42 (m,
2H), 3.37-3.30 (m, 3H), 2.20-2.11 (m, 2H), 2.07-1.95 (m, 2H), 1.70-1.62
(m, 2H), 1.55-1.36 (m, 5H), 0.99 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H); MS m/z 441.30
[M+H]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation, microwave tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
