$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of 2-Methoxypyidine-4-boronic Acid Pinacol Ester (15). A
solution of 4-bromo-2-methoxypyridine (14) (462 mg, 2.46 mmol, 1.0
equiv), bis(pinacolato)diboron (749 mg, 2.95 mmol, 1.2 equiv),
PdCl2(dppf) (54 mg, 0.074 mmol, 3 mol %), and KOAc (724 mg, 7.37 mmol,
3.0 equiv) in DMF (6 mL) in a resealable pressure vessel was degassed
through bubbling nitrogen for 20 min. The reaction mixture was sealed and
heated over a sand bath at 85 °C overnight. After cooling to room
temperature, the mixture was diluted with EtOAc and filtered through a
plug of Celite and anhydrous Na2SO4. The solvent was removed in vacuo,
and the residue was purified by flash chromatography on silica gel using
EtOAc-MeOH as the eluent to provide 15. Brownish oil, yield 427.4 mg,
74%. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.34 (s, 12H), 3.93 (s, 3H), 7.13 (s, 1H),
7.18 (d, J= 5.0 Hz, 1H), 8.18 (d, J= 5.0 Hz, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Suzuki-Miyaura coupling, sealed pressure vessel used
